            "status": "introduced",
            "necessary": "yes",
            "before": {
              "requirement": "Provide a 32-element z_crc_t operator array to crc32_combine_gen(op, len2), then pass that array to crc32_combine_op.",
              "applicability": "required",
              "harness_status": "sat",
              "reason": "The old harness allocates the required array and uses the former generator and operator signatures.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-89c91b53dc675dcff0b52078",
                  "quote": "ZEXTERN void ZEXPORT crc32_combine_gen OF((z_crc_t op[32], z_off_t len2));\n     Generate the operator op corresponding to length len2, to be used with\n   crc32_combine_op(). op must have room for 32 z_crc_t values. (32 is the\n   number of bits in the CRC.)\nZEXTERN uLong ZEXPORT crc32_combine_op OF((uLong crc1, uLong crc2,\n                                           const z_crc_t *op));\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-d78dfa71b3aecae254ced71c",
                  "quote": "void ZEXPORT crc32_combine_gen(op, len2)\n    z_crc_t *op;\n    z_off_t len2;\n{\n    crc32_combine_gen_(op, len2);\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-c495faf56bf071b79046603c",
                  "quote": "uLong crc32_combine_op(crc1, crc2, op)\n    uLong crc1;\n    uLong crc2;\n    const z_crc_t *op;\n{\n    return gf2_matrix_times(op, crc1) ^ crc2;\n}\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "after": {
              "requirement": "Use the uLong returned by crc32_combine_gen(len2) as the scalar operator passed to crc32_combine_op.",
              "applicability": "required",
              "harness_status": "unsat",
              "reason": "The fixed old harness passes two arguments to the one-argument generator and passes an array to the scalar operator.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-8c10a0d35e8413a0c91a1e02",
                  "quote": "ZEXTERN uLong ZEXPORT crc32_combine_gen OF((z_off_t len2));\n     Return the operator corresponding to length len2, to be used with\n   crc32_combine_op().\nZEXTERN uLong ZEXPORT crc32_combine_op OF((uLong crc1, uLong crc2, uLong op));\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-a404f0762bc5f0c5b3359fe7",
                  "quote": "uLong ZEXPORT crc32_combine_gen(len2)\n    z_off_t len2;\n{\n    return crc32_combine_gen64(len2);\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-ee21c29f027cb267a71a78c7",
                  "quote": "uLong crc32_combine_op(crc1, crc2, op)\n    uLong crc1;\n    uLong crc2;\n    uLong op;\n{\n    return multmodp(op, crc1) ^ crc2;\n}\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "same_blocker": "not_applicable",
            "reason": "The same CRC combine operation is compatible before and incompatible after because its operator representation changed.",
